{"id": "EUVD-2026-48927", "enisaUuid": "d66f96e0-2bf8-3651-81bb-c81b1f16847c", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb: client: fix double-free in SMB2_flush() replay\n\nSMB2_flush() keeps its response buffer bookkeeping across replay\nattempts. If a replayable flush response is received and the retry then\nfails before cifs_send_recv() stores a replacement response, flush_exit\nwill free the stale response pointer a second time.\n\nReinitialize resp_buftype and rsp_iov at the top of the replay loop so\ncleanup only acts on response state produced by the current attempt.\nThis fixes a double-free without changing replay handling for successful\nrequests.", "datePublished": "2026-07-25T08:50:32", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T20:38:26", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6e27f40b682a5e42a2daae3ce6d96f0e0e16dedb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/878757163eea684750107a31ea134c103863515d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3407240cde132a4b72d6429a2625a09a2f78adaf", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/013a9a3da46c5dabcf18f65ea6a47874ba12a15d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4be31c943a3a27a5a0251dbb8f5cb89059ec3d5a"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-64383", "GHSA-j3g4-c7cw-5ch7"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.46, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "133f724d-69c0-3d43-85ac-60e543949ac5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4f1fffa2376922f3d1d506e49c0fd445b023a28e <013a9a3da46c5dabcf18f65ea6a47874ba12a15d"}, {"id": "158f8766-cefa-3a8e-94ab-63e5b19107a9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "433042a91f9373241307725b52de573933ffedbf <6e27f40b682a5e42a2daae3ce6d96f0e0e16dedb"}, {"id": "247f9707-f190-3bd9-ac8a-1ee74c24d5b7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6.32 <6.6.145"}, {"id": "311c4cd8-a74c-35a2-b3fe-1c89efeaf1ba", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "450b7a30-a775-3216-89f0-29bcb6b5aac6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.8"}, {"id": "764f62a4-5648-3896-9a13-6bb4323262b0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.96"}, {"id": "7e45fdaf-c843-3df2-8a4c-ebada38f0c3f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.39"}, {"id": "c15d22aa-1133-3e37-8273-a088871f7484", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.4"}, {"id": "cba251fc-0bcb-33d6-b687-276f70d5a63e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.145"}, {"id": "d62255e6-d7a5-3142-aff9-40b074b6ca50", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4f1fffa2376922f3d1d506e49c0fd445b023a28e <878757163eea684750107a31ea134c103863515d"}, {"id": "dc7d8197-474b-3c17-9320-e6330b9a93a7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4f1fffa2376922f3d1d506e49c0fd445b023a28e <3407240cde132a4b72d6429a2625a09a2f78adaf"}, {"id": "f7be061a-c3b3-3e3b-a2f5-1c3529decd46", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4f1fffa2376922f3d1d506e49c0fd445b023a28e <4be31c943a3a27a5a0251dbb8f5cb89059ec3d5a"}, {"id": "ff801052-d891-3e11-a55d-d2a84bbce18a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "9d590c52-7d93-3e11-9b49-6f90ccda5475", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}